# Mechan Shieldmate {1}{U} 3/2, Defender: "As long as an artifact entered the battlefield under your control this turn, this creature can attack as though it
# didn't have defender." Bot1 casts it turn 1 with two Moxen, then an Ornithopter (the control attacker: it keeps the declaration step happening). Turn 3: no
# artifact entered under Bot1's control this turn, so the Shieldmate cannot attack (Bot2's Ornithopter, cast on turn 2, is no help: another turn and another
# player's) while the Ornithopter can. Turn 5: Bot1 casts Sol Ring, so the Shieldmate can attack and deals 3. Turn 7: the Sol Ring entered on an earlier turn,
# so it cannot attack again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mechan Shieldmate
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Island x3
Forest
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mechan Shieldmate.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mechan Shieldmate.Keywords = Defender
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Attack(Mechan Shieldmate > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Mechan Shieldmate > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Attack(Mechan Shieldmate > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Mechan Shieldmate.Tapped = false
